# Customer Engagement

First product module. Spec: `docs/features/customer-engagement.md`. UX and approved decisions: `docs/architecture/`. Usage: `docs/features/customer-usage.md` (do not build yet).

## Purpose

Administrators author **rule definitions**: eligibility, template, timing, status. Real-time validation is required. Recipient preview is out of scope.

v1 intended send behaviour (backend, not Angular): **once per customer per qualifying occurrence**. Do not implement evaluation, deduplication, send history, or email.

## Build in the frontend

- Rule list and editor (v1: one AND/OR group; nested groups in the model only).
- Extensible metric catalog and separate **rule** category catalog.
- Read-only system template **selection** (not an email composer; no create/edit/activate).
- Timing: on match, or X days before/after catalog lifecycle anchors.
- Save-blocking validation. Mock services behind contracts.

## Do not build

- Email sending, Postmark, evaluation of customers, scheduling, or delivery.
- Customer targeting / recipient preview.
- Customer Usage dashboards or “coming soon” nav.
- Frequency / cooldown / re-entry / history UI.
- Database schemas or backend workflows.

## Architecture

Share metric contracts so Usage can later display the same signals. Keep trial/account enum values **centralised** as temporary mock contracts. Condition fields and rule categories are catalog-driven.
